  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1204 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nThrough this weekend, much of the CONUS east of the Rockies is \nforecast to remain in broad troughing at 500 MB, a weak \nshortwave is forecast to move across the area Friday night into \nearly Saturday morning and bring the chance of sprinkles or \nflurries to the area. Saturday is expected to be noticeably \nwarmer with high temperatures in the lower to mid 50s as weak \nhigh pressure quickly moves across the area.\n\nAnother shortwave is forecast to drop into the trough and move\nacross the area Saturday night through the day on Sunday\nbringing another round of rain and possibly a rain/snow mix to \nthe area as precipitation comes to an end on Sunday morning. \nHigh temperatures on Sunday are expected to occur early in the \nmorning with temperatures holding in the upper 30s to lower 40s \nduring the day. Model ensembles have trended faster in recent \nruns with this system than their operational counterparts along \nwith increasing QPF with the NBM lagging these current trends. \nRainfall amounts up to a quarter of an inch are possible.\n\nMonday and beyond, models show a broad zonal flow across the US\nthrough the middle of next week with a gradual warming trend.\nThere is a potential for a shortwave moving through the flow to\nbring precipitation by midweek, but there is low confidence on \nits timing and locations with some models taking this shortwave \nto the south of the area.",
